  "title": "Kirby Problem 1.64",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "(a) Let $L \\subset (S^{3}, \\xi_{std})$ be a transverse link such that the branched double cover\n$(\\Sigma_{2}(L), \\xi_{L})$ is Stein fillable. Is $L$ transversely isotopic to the closure of a\nquasipositive braid?\n(b) Is the same true if $(\\Sigma_{n}(L), \\xi_{L})$ is Stein fillable for some $n > 2$?\n(c) Does Stein fillability of the branched cover imply that the slice-Bennequin\ninequality must be sharp for the given link?",
